course: dictionary
lesson: 10400
title: The triceps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your arm moves because of muscles. A muscle can only pull, never push, so muscles work in pairs. «The biceps bends the arm and the triceps straightens it.» The biceps is at the front of your upper arm and the triceps is at the back.
explain: The triceps is the big muscle at the back of your upper arm. When it pulls, it straightens your arm at the elbow. «Straighten it and the triceps at the back pulls it down again.» Feel it by bending your arm, then straightening it.
explain: Both muscles are needed. The biceps and the triceps are partners that pull in opposite directions. «When you bend your arm the biceps at the front pulls, and to straighten it the triceps at the back pulls.»
fact: The triceps is at the back of the upper arm.
fact: The triceps straightens your arm at the elbow.
fact: A muscle can only pull, never push.
fact: The biceps and the triceps work in pairs, pulling in opposite directions.
fact: Push-ups are an exercise that works the triceps.
exercise: «Bend your arm and feel the biceps at the front go hard.» What does the triceps do? | Bends the arm at the elbow | *Straightens the arm at the elbow | Lifts the head | Makes the hand grip tighter
exercise: Why do muscles work in pairs? | Because bones need company | Because muscles can push and pull | *Because a muscle can only pull, so another muscle is needed to undo the movement | Because the biceps is bigger than the triceps
exercise: «The biceps bends the arm and the triceps straightens it.» Find and copy the name of the muscle that straightens the arm. | elbow | arm | *triceps | biceps
test: Where is the triceps? | In the stomach | *At the back of the upper arm | In the hand | At the front of the upper arm
test: Which exercise works the triceps? | Sleeping | Reading a book | *Push-ups | Singing
exam: «A muscle can only pull, never push.» If the triceps pulls, what happens to your arm? | Your arm turns around | Your arm gets longer | *Your arm straightens at the elbow | Your arm bends at the elbow
